 :carried-selectors-that-cannot-discriminate
 {:found "2026-09-10, by running the component's own oracle-expand over every selector"
  :measured
  {0 303754089 1 499508843 2 701086944 3 499508843 4 303754089 5 499508843}
  :finding
  "Selector 4 is the `expand BOTH refs` case, carried from the abb_robotics
   sibling whose BOM spec genuinely declares two. No accela spec has two refs,
   so selector 4 asks for \"projectId,projectId\" and returns EXACTLY selector
   0's value. It cannot tell a fold that ran twice from one that ran once, and
   in the sibling that same selector IS distinct (728485347 against 253212778).

   This is the class :generated-not-hand-ported says cannot be carried. The
   generator does derive the TABLES from entity-specs, and those are right --
   what it still templates is the oracle SELECTORS, and one of them names a
   shape this entity table does not have."
  :also
  {:cred-row
   "Emits \"projectId\" twice -- a duplicate JSON key -- and a \"quantity\"
    field that no accela spec declares. Both survived `amu check :ok true`,
    because the object is built with `jkv` calls and the compiler has no schema
    for it. A green check is not evidence that a fixture is well formed."}
  :not-fixed-here
  "The file is generated. Hand-patching its output would make the next
   regeneration silently undo the fix, so the repair belongs in
   scripts/gen-whole-component.cljs -- derive the expand selectors from the ref
   arity of the entity being generated, and build cred-row from the spec's own
   field list."}

 :regenerated-2026-09-10
 {:generator "kotoba-lang scripts/gen-whole-component.cljs, after the ref-arity fix"
  :closes "the two defects recorded above under :carried-selectors-that-cannot-discriminate"
  :cred-row "now id + the one ref field + two of the spec's own required fields. No duplicate key, and no `quantity` -- a field no accela spec declares."
  :oracle-expand "selector 4 is not generated, and the file says why: one ref means a BOTH case would duplicate selector 0."
  :measured
